WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.140
Your first microservice is a joy.

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.740
Your tenth is a warning.

3
00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.050
So, what changed?

4
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.740
Every service needs the same non-business things.

5
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.270
Knowing who's calling.

6
00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:15.630
Logging the same way.

7
00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:16.670
Retrying safely.

8
00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.040
Resolving the tenant.

9
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.300
Returning the same error shape.

10
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.140
None of that is your product.

11
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.530
All of it is horizontal

12
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.640
— it cuts across every service.

13
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:30.020
Now copy that right-hand column into ten repositories.

14
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.260
Written ten slightly different ways,

15
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.300
by ten people, over two years.

16
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.840
That's not architecture.

17
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.470
That's ten liabilities.

18
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.190
Take one concept:

19
00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.020
reading the current user.

20
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.340
Three repositories.

21
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:44.270
Three near-identical versions.

22
00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.450
Every one of them has drifted.

23
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.810
A security fix becomes a ten-repository pull request.

24
00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.180
That's the tax.

25
00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.930
The cost of microservices is rarely the services.

26
00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.160
It's the duplication of everything around them.

27
00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.050
Fixing that needs two ideas:

28
00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.730
a cleaner definition of what a service is,

29
00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.530
and a home for all the horizontal stuff.

30
00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:07.510
Next:

31
00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:08.430
the first idea

32
00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.440
— a service is a contract, not a codebase.
